{"id":"57d0f312ae9a795b","group":"58","path":"58/batch08/58-thm-covering-lemma.md","title":"Jensen Covering Lemma","display":"thm-covering-lemma — Jensen Covering Lemma","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-covering-lemma","aliases":["58-thm-covering-lemma","Jensen Covering Lemma","Covering Lemma for L"],"display":"thm-covering-lemma — Jensen Covering Lemma","depends_on":["[[../batch02/58-thm-0-sharp.md]]","[[../batch10/58-thm-L-condensation.md]]","[[58-df-elementary-substructure.md]]","[[../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-covering-lemma"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-covering-lemma</span><span>Jensen Covering Lemma</span><span>Covering Lemma for L</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-covering-lemma — Jensen Covering Lemma"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"16b215b0ea9d456b\" href=\"?note=16b215b0ea9d456b\" title=\"../batch02/58-thm-0-sharp.md\">../batch02/58-thm-0-sharp.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"2331ede3868d950e\" href=\"?note=2331ede3868d950e\" title=\"../batch10/58-thm-L-condensation.md\">../batch10/58-thm-L-condensation.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"faf104362ffe13b3\" href=\"?note=faf104362ffe13b3\" title=\"58-df-elementary-substructure.md\">58-df-elementary-substructure.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"5582a281f15a33c2\" href=\"?note=5582a281f15a33c2\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md\">../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X,Y\\in V\">\\(X,Y\\in V\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Ordinal}:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Ordinal}:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> is the ordinal predicate</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Exists}(0^\\sharp)\\in\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Exists}(0^\\sharp)\\in\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> is the zero-sharp existence sentence (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"16b215b0ea9d456b\" href=\"?note=16b215b0ea9d456b\" title=\"../batch02/58-thm-0-sharp.md\">../batch02/58-thm-0-sharp.md</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}covering\\text{-}lemma} \\vdash\n\\neg\\mathrm{Exists}(0^\\sharp)\n\\to\n\\forall X\\in V\\;\n\\bigl(\n(\\forall\\xi\\in X\\;\\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\xi))\\land |X| &gt; \\aleph_0 \\rightarrow\n\\exists Y \\in L\\;(X \\subseteq Y \\land |Y| = |X|)\n\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}covering\\text{-}lemma} \\vdash\n\\neg\\mathrm{Exists}(0^\\sharp)\n\\to\n\\forall X\\in V\\;\n\\bigl(\n(\\forall\\xi\\in X\\;\\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\xi))\\land |X| &gt; \\aleph_0 \\rightarrow\n\\exists Y \\in L\\;(X \\subseteq Y \\land |Y| = |X|)\n\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This is the standard covering property of <code>L</code> in the absence of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"0^\\#\">\\(0^\\#\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The quantifier <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\\subseteq\\mathrm{Ord}\">\\(X\\subseteq\\mathrm{Ord}\\)</span> ranges over sets of ordinals; it does not quantify over proper subclasses.</li>\n<li>A common consequence is that singular cardinals in <code>V</code> remain singular in <code>L</code>, and for singular <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span> one has <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(\\kappa^+)^L = \\kappa^+\">\\((\\kappa^+)^L = \\kappa^+\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>If <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"0^\\#\">\\(0^\\#\\)</span> exists, this covering phenomenon fails.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch02/58-thm-0-sharp.md","status":"resolved","id":"16b215b0ea9d456b","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-thm-0-sharp.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch10/58-thm-L-condensation.md","status":"resolved","id":"2331ede3868d950e","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch10/58-thm-L-condensation.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-elementary-substructure.md","status":"resolved","id":"faf104362ffe13b3","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-elementary-substructure.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md","status":"resolved","id":"5582a281f15a33c2","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-thm-0-sharp.md","status":"resolved","id":"16b215b0ea9d456b","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Exists}(0^\\sharp)\\in\\{\\top,\\bot\\}$ is the zero-sharp existence sentence (see [[../batch02/58-thm-0-sharp.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"X,Y\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Ordinal}:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Exists}(0^\\sharp)\\in\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}covering\\text{-}lemma} \\vdash\n\\neg\\mathrm{Exists}(0^\\sharp)\n\\to\n\\forall X\\in V\\;\n\\bigl(\n(\\forall\\xi\\in X\\;\\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\xi))\\land |X| > \\aleph_0 \\rightarrow\n\\exists Y \\in L\\;(X \\subseteq Y \\land |Y| = |X|)\n\\bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"0^\\#","display":false},{"tex":"X\\subseteq\\mathrm{Ord}","display":false},{"tex":"\\kappa","display":false},{"tex":"(\\kappa^+)^L = \\kappa^+","display":false},{"tex":"0^\\#","display":false}],"bytes":1328,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4102","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch08/58-thm-covering-lemma.md|58-thm-covering-lemma]]（batch08）"},{"id":"7334957c6d59eacc","anchor":"ref-170","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[58-thm-0-sharp.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-condensation.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-definability.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-generic-extension.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-is-transitive.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-satisfies-GCH.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-satisfies-ZFC.md]]\n[[58-thm-MM.md]]\n[[58-thm-V-equal-L.md]]\n[[58-thm-V-equals-L.md]]\n[[58-thm-absoluteness-calculation.md]]\n[[58-thm-ac-wellorder-equivalent.md]]\n[[58-thm-aleph-properties.md]]\n[[58-thm-analytic-completeness.md]]\n[[58-thm-analytic-set-properties.md]]\n[[58-thm-baire-category-theory.md]]\n[[58-thm-baire-category.md]]\n[[58-thm-banach-tarski.md]]\n[[58-thm-beth-function-properties.md]]\n[[58-thm-boolean-valued-model.md]]\n[[58-thm-borel-cardinality.md]]\n[[58-thm-borel-determinacy-proof.md]]\n[[58-thm-bounded-forcing-axioms.md]]\n[[58-thm-cantor.md]]\n[[58-thm-cardinal-multiplication.md]]\n[[58-thm-club-filter-properties.md]]\n[[58-thm-club-guessing.md]]\n[[58-thm-club-intersection-proper.md]]\n[[58-thm-club-intersection.md]]\n[[58-thm-coanalytic-separation.md]]\n[[58-thm-coding-universe.md]]\n[[58-thm-cofinality-regular.md]]\n[[58-thm-cohen-forcing-CH.md]]\n[[58-thm-collapse-forcing.md]]\n[[58-thm-compactness.md]]\n[[58-thm-consistency-strength-hierarchy.md]]\n[[58-thm-continuum-hypothesis.md]]\n[[58-thm-countable-choice.md]]\n[[58-thm-covering-lemma.md]]\n[[58-thm-dense-set-lemma.md]]\n[[58-thm-dependent-choice.md]]\n[[58-thm-determinacy.md]]\n[[58-thm-diamond-implies-CH.md]]\n[[58-thm-diamond-properties.md]]\n[[58-thm-easton-forci